            <ArticleTitle>C to T and/or G to A transitions are responsible for loss of a MspI restriction site at the 5'-end of the human apolipoprotein AI gene.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>473-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We detected the loss of a MspI restriction site by a C to T transition at +83 bp and a G to A transition at +84 bp of the 5'-end non-coding region of the human apolipoprotein AI gene. This base change occurred at the &quot;hot spot&quot; (CCGG) for methylation, which may be important in the regulation of gene expression. The population frequency for the loss of the MspI site is 6.1%.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
